# One Type Per File

- Every nontrivial type (`class`, `interface`, `struct`, `enum`, `record`) gets its own source file
- The file name must match the type name (e.g. `UserApplicationService.cs` for `UserApplicationService`)
- Do not combine multiple nontrivial types in one file
- Nested types are allowed only when they are trivial implementation details of the enclosing type
- Entry points such as `Program.cs` may remain minimal bootstrap code only
